*  CN-12 -- a SINGLE-WRITE BARE VAR as a cset argument folds through the same
*  inference the PT-1/PT-3 pattern inline already trusts (sno_var_val: wrcount==1,
*  fz-safe, seal-table storage).  This is beauty's load-bearing shape: its grammar
*  csets name digits/nl/tab, and the DIGITS leaf alone was measured (s161-2) to be
*  the whole reason SPAN('.' digits &UCASE '_' &LCASE) declined.
	&USER_DECLARED_CONSTANTS = 1
	t = "b"
	&W = SPAN("a" t)
	"abba x" POS(0) *&W	:S(Y)F(N)
Y	OUTPUT = "match"	:(END)
N	OUTPUT = "nomatch"
END
